      "content": "it's more than just \"potential\" for me. i've been tracking the peaks and they line up exactly with when the local council meetings happen or when there's a town hall scheduled. it's like they're preemptively dampening the energy in the room so no one gets too vocal or aggressive about the new zoning laws. if you look at the specific modulation i'm seeing, it's almost a perfect sine wave sink at 7hz. what would be the strategic advantage of hitting that specific frequency during a public gathering?",
